			"date": "2024-02-18T06:25:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> unpopular opinion: they’re right. It’s true that this exposes a security issue, and it’s true that PWAs are not popular. I work in the field, and never, I repeat never, met a person with a PWA installed. One of most popular app in Italy is one that JUST makes n/1.22 to make a tax calculation, it’s an App!!! And I will believe they’re evil when they’ll do a layoff. Other companies are doing it yearly, even Mozilla and other good-ish companies, they are at zero count yet.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
